Trim the level2/coco3/cmds Makefile to only what assembles cleanly
under current lwasm with a stock NitrOS-9 v3.3.0 source tree (no
3rdparty packages present).

- Drop `edit`: source uses `pulu pc,u` / `pshu u`, which lwasm
  rejects as ambiguous on the 6809 (you can't push/pull U via
  the user stack since U is the stack pointer for that mode).
- Drop CMDS_D2 third-party tools: basic09, runb, gfx2, gfx,
  inkey, syscall, tmode -- source lives under 3rdparty/packages/
  which isn't in the stock v3.3.0 archive.
- Drop CMDS_DW: inetd, dw, telnet, httpd are also 3rdparty.

What's left is more than enough to boot, log in, and run the WiFi
telnet bridge.

--- a/level2/coco3/cmds/Makefile
+++ b/level2/coco3/cmds/Makefile
@@ -16,17 +16,17 @@
 
 CMDS		= asm attr backup binex build cmp cobbler copy cputype \
 		date dcheck debug ded deiniz del deldir devs dir dirsort disasm \
-		display dmem dmode dsave dump echo edit error exbin \
+		display dmem dmode dsave dump echo error exbin \
 		format free grfdrv help ident iniz irqs link list load login \
 		makdir mdir megaread merge mfree minted mmap modpatch montype mpi os9gen padrom park \
 		pmap proc procs prompt pwd pxd reboot rename save setime \
 		shell_21 sleep smap tee tmode touch tsmon tuneport unlink verify wcreate xmode
 
-CMDS_D2         = basic09 runb gfx2 gfx inkey syscall copy del echo format \
-                merge os9gen prompt tmode
+CMDS_D2 = copy del echo format merge os9gen prompt
 
-CMDS_DW		= inetd dw telnet httpd
 
+CMDS_DW =
+
 SHELLMODS	= shellplus date deiniz echo iniz link load save unlink
 
 UTILPAK1	= attr build copy del deldir dir display list makdir mdir \
